Company Description Eckstein Engineering Business Solutions focuses on delivering high-quality engineering services that enable global organizations to leverage India's technical talent and cost advantages. The company partners with international clients to design, implement, and support advanced automation and control systems. By combining deep domain expertise with a commitment to reliability and innovation, Eckstein Engineering Business Solutions helps organizations optimize processes and improve operational performance. Team members can expect exposure to global standards, diverse projects, and opportunities to work with leading industrial technologies. The organization values professional growth, collaboration, and long-term client relationships. 

Role Description This is a full-time, on-site PLC-Automation Engineer position based in Pune City. The role involves designing, programming, and commissioning automation solutions using CODESYS, TwinCAT, and Siemens TIA Portal/Schneider platforms for industrial and process control applications. Day-to-day responsibilities include developing PLC logic, HMI/SCADA configurations, testing and debugging control programs, and ensuring seamless integration with electrical and mechanical systems. The engineer will collaborate with cross-functional teams to gather requirements, create technical documentation, and support installation, start-up, and optimization of automated systems at customer sites. The role also includes diagnosing issues, performing root-cause analysis, implementing corrective actions, and maintaining compliance with relevant safety and industry standards. 

Qualifications

- Strong automation and process control skills, including hands-on experience with PLC programming and industrial control systems. 
 - Solid electrical engineering knowledge for interpreting schematics, wiring diagrams, and integrating control hardware. 
 - Proficiency in troubleshooting and diagnostics for PLCs, field devices, communication networks, and control loops. 
 - Experience with robotics or motion control systems and their integration with PLC-based architectures. 
 - Minimum 8 years of experience working with CODESYS, TwinCAT, and Siemens TIA Portal/Schneider platforms in industrial environments. 
 - Ability to create clear technical documentation, including functional specifications, I/O lists, and test protocols. 
 - Familiarity with industrial communication protocols (e. g. , Modbus, Profinet, EtherCAT) and safety PLC concepts. 
 - Bachelor's degree in Electrical, Electronics, Instrumentation, or related engineering discipline, or equivalent practical experience. 
 - Effective communication skills and ability to collaborate with multidisciplinary teams and clients on-site. 
 - Willingness to work on shop floors and customer locations as required, adhering to all safety and quality practices.

