About Intrida&nbsp; 

You probably haven't heard of Intrida yet. We're a growing technology company that has been quietly building something with big ambitions. &nbsp; 

Headquartered in Cambridge, UK, with an international team, we have developed a software platform, called XcheckStudio (XCS), that helps companies bring together, validate and manage the data generated by complex projects, including 3D models, drawings, documents and databases. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

About the QA Engineer Role&nbsp; 

As a QA Engineer in our Pune office, you'll quickly become an important part of the QA team. 

This is a hands-on role combining software QA, product validation and engineering application testing. You'll help test new and existing features, investigate issues and validate how XcheckStudio works in real-world engineering scenarios. &nbsp; 

You'll also have the opportunity to work with sample projects, customer scenarios, Proof of Concepts and product demonstrations as you develop your understanding of the XcheckStudio platform. 

&nbsp; 

What You'll Do&nbsp; 

- Carry out software testing and product validation activities. &nbsp; 
 - Identify, investigate and document product issues and follow them through to resolution. &nbsp; 
 - Work closely with developers and other technical colleagues. &nbsp; 
 - Record and report testing and validation results. &nbsp; 
 - Help validate real-world engineering workflows and customer scenarios. &nbsp; 
 - Support Proof of Concept deployments and product demonstrations. &nbsp; 
 - Contribute to improving QA processes and documentation. &nbsp; 
 - Participate in Agile/Scrum development and QA meetings. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

What We're Looking For&nbsp; 

We're looking for someone with 2-4 years of professional experience who is technically minded, curious and keen to develop their skills

&nbsp; 

Essential&nbsp; 

- Bachelor's degree or equivalent in Engineering, Computer Science, Science or a related technical discipline. &nbsp; 
 - Experience in QA, software testing, applications engineering or a similar technical role. &nbsp; 
 - Experience working with technical, engineering or enterprise software applications. &nbsp; 
 - Understanding of software QA and testing principles. &nbsp; 
 - Strong problem-solving and investigative skills. &nbsp; 
 - Good attention to detail and a methodical approach. &nbsp; 
 - Good written and spoken English. &nbsp; 
 - Ability to work collaboratively and take ownership of tasks. &nbsp; Desirable&nbsp; 

- Selenium or another automated testing framework. &nbsp; 
 - Python or another scripting language. &nbsp; 
 - Cloud-based applications or deployment environments. &nbsp; 
 - Agile/Scrum experience. &nbsp; 
 - Issue tracking or test management systems. &nbsp; 
 - Interest in using AI-enabled tools in software development and QA. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

Why Join Intrida?&nbsp; 

- Contribute directly to the development of our own platform, XcheckStudio. &nbsp; 
 - Develop your technical and QA skills within a growing technology company. &nbsp; 
 - Work with colleagues and customers across the UK, India and international markets. &nbsp; 
 - Join a close-knit team where ideas, ownership and learning are encouraged. &nbsp; 
 - Potential opportunities for international travel as we grow. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

The Process

