 - Experience implementing and supporting High Availability (HA) and Disaster Recovery (DR) technologies, including emerging solutions and best practices. &nbsp; 
 - Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to resolve complex software and interface-related issues. &nbsp; 
 - Demonstrated willingness to take ownership, accept responsibility, and be accountable for service delivery outcomes. &nbsp; 
 - Sound knowledge of Microsoft Office applications and Power BI. &nbsp; 
 - Strong documentation skills, with the ability to create and maintain technical and operational documentation. &nbsp; 
Personal Attributes

- Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to engage stakeholders at all levels of the organisation and build trusted relationships with clients and internal stakeholders. &nbsp; 
 - Experience within the Superannuation industry or, preferably, the broader Financial Services sector. &nbsp; 
 - Availability to provide on-call support and work flexible shifts in line with business and operational requirements. 
 - Highly effective communication, collaboration, and influencing skills. &nbsp; 
 - Demonstrated willingness to take ownership, accept responsibility, and be accountable for service delivery outcomes. &nbsp; 
 - Strong leadership capabilities with a focus on coaching, mentoring, and developing high-performing teams. &nbsp; 
 - Demonstrates flexibility and adaptability to meet evolving business and operational requirements. 
 - Effective verbal and written communication skills.

